  "question": {
    "text": "A thin non conducting disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is placed on a frictionless horizontal plane with its centre at the origin of the coordinate system. A non-uniform, radial magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> exists in space, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> is a unit vector in the radially outward direction. The disc is set in motion with an angular velocity <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, about an axis passing through its centre and perpendicular to its plane, as shown in the figure. At what value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, the disc will lift off from the surface.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image12-b6c5ec03-d868-4606-aba8-f279e3613e94.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 160px; width: 230px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The force an any small part of the disc is in the vertically upward direction<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math><br /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image13-f1c969e8-2738-4a95-97ae-da0bfe4a1b28.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" /><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
